                <pb facs="0297" n="195" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg195"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/2425: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morrow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-11-17T18:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                                1927—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8: 58
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>412. The Supreme Court rendered decision today which is reported to hold articles
                    14 and 15 of petroleum law unconstitutional. Will report fully when copy of
                    decision is obtained.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morrow</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
